Chapter 10: “The Lion King’s Land”
Chapter 10, Section 22: “Preparations and Refusal”

――This scene took place in the commercial district of the Royal Capital of Lugunica, at the very same time that Natsuki Subaru, in the hideout of the “Six Tongues,” was being informed of the colossal danger threatening the Kingdom of Lugunica.

“――By some means or another, the enemy has already gotten their hands on the Dragon History Stone and seized full authority. That is the situation the Royal Castle currently finds itself in. I have filled in the missing pieces of information with my own conjectures, but I doubt they are far off the mark.”

“……Indeed. It also explains why we are currently being hunted. At the very least, we should assume that the chain of command within the Royal Castle has already been compromised.”

“――――”

“Garfiel, are you alright?”

“Huh? Y-yeah, I’m fine… Nah, honestly, it’s just a scale of trouble I never even imagined, so… I just don’t know what to say.”

Shaking his head in denial, Garfiel confesses his painfully honest feelings. However, Otto understood his junior’s feelings; it was only natural.

“……Given the situation, that is.”

Frankly speaking, Otto was equally racking his brains over the chaos and confusion. It was simply that, due to the differences in their roles within the camp, Otto was not permitted to stop thinking.

In this desperate situation, Garfiel had properly fulfilled his role. ――No, not just Garfiel. It was the result of everyone uniting as one and giving their all.

The only one who failed was the pathetic one who had his weapon taken away: himself.

“――Tch.”

Leaning his back against the wall of the room, hugging one knee as he sat, Garfiel groaned in pain from his throat.

The intense exhaustion and pain etched on his face showed no sign of fading, a state unthinkable for Garfiel, who possessed absurd toughness and recovery. This was a testament to how irregular and unreasonable the power of the one who landed a blow on him – Reinhard – truly was.

――It had been some time since Reinhard had blocked Otto and the others, and they had barely managed to break through, using every card they had.

The battle itself had lasted less than a minute, but by its end, everyone was battered and bruised. In particular, Garfiel, who had faced Reinhard head-on, was in terrible shape. Otto felt pathetic; even though he’d deliberately baited the opponent’s carelessness, a mere graze to the jaw had rendered him immobile.

The victory they had barely snatched away was only possible thanks to unexpected reinforcements. Including the fact that the situation had developed that way at all, Otto had far too much to reflect upon.

The only reason they could afford something resembling a reflection meeting was because they had been led by the arriving reinforcements and secured a temporary safe haven like this.

“……The fact that ye managed to shake him off is remarkable in itself. Even if it was a role forced upon him unwillingly, a hundred ordinary soldiers could do naught against him.”

“However, to do so, we forced her to use a card that should not have been used. What she cast away from her own life was immense. I cannot forgive that person.”

“……Your anger is more than justified. He's likely prepared to be resented. That is what it means to be the ‘Sword Saint.’ Even I have never lost my anger towards the ‘Sword Saint.’”

“That is…”

Otto quietly narrowed his eyes at the person who placed a large hand upon his own bald head.

What he had been about to say, be it a question or speculation, was swallowed back, as he realized he’d already said something he shouldn’t have.

However――

“――You must mean your anger towards my wife, not Reinhard.”

The one who took the words from the now-silent Otto, in a tone filled with certainty, was the old swordsman who opened the entrance door――Wilhelm.

Entering the room, Wilhelm was accompanied by Rem and a short-haired elderly man. He let Rem enter the room first, then turned to the man,

“Conwood, I apologize for the trouble. I am in your debt for sheltering us.”

“Hah, to think the day would come when Wilhelm Trias, the very epitome of arrogance and selfishness, would give me such an admirably grateful thanks. It might rain tomorrow.”

“You…”

“It’s a joke. ――Besides, this is only natural. It’s only natural, Wilhelm. Me lending you a hand… that’s just a matter of course, not something that requires thanks.”

“――――”

After the familiar tone, Wilhelm’s cheeks stiffened at the man whose voice trembled with emotion.

The man, seeming amused by the reaction of his old acquaintance, relaxed his cheeks. Then, looking at Otto and Garfiel inside the room,

“I owe a debt to your comrade, Natsuki Subaru, from the time of the White Whale subjugation. A debt so huge it would take a lifetime to repay. I won’t let anyone pass here, so rest easy.”

“……Master, you have our gratitude.”

“I told you. The gratitude is far greater on my side. …No one believes Natsuki Subaru-sama is part of the Witch’s Cult. It’s the same for Crusch-sama.”

With those words, the man clapped Wilhelm on the shoulder and left, closing the door behind him. Watching his back disappear behind the door, Otto called out, “Rem-san.”

This place they had arrived at under Wilhelm’s guidance was a private room in a tavern offered as a refuge. While Otto and the others were explaining their situation in this room, Rem had been in a separate room.

The reason for that was――

“Were Petra-chan and the others alright?”

“……They are resting, for now. Petra-chan was quite distraught, and Meili-chan was the one comforting her, but… they have both fallen asleep.”

“Is that so… Understood. Thank you very much.”

“No, I did nothing. More importantly, what about the discussion?”

“We’ve just finished confirming the current situation, I suppose.”

Otto replied to the tense-faced Rem, directing his light-blue eyes toward the back of the room.

Following her gaze, standing there was a large figure seated in the private room who still had his head higher than Otto or Wilhelm’s.

A bald head, a giant old frame with sun-tanned skin, his name was――

“――Barga Cromwell. One of the main figures who escalated the kingdom’s civil war in the past.”

“……Unfortunately, I don’t know who you’re talking about. I’m just Old Man Rom, a large old fart who lived in the slums, nothing more.”

“How brazen you are. What happened to the scar I gouged into your chest? Are you hiding it under that magnificent white chest hair?”

“I understand even less what you mean. Even if it’s not about me, I wouldn’t wish for old age. Seems even that famed ‘Sword Demon’ can’t match the wits of advancing years, eh?”

“You scoundrel――”

“……Both of you, please stop fighting. Petra-chan and the others are resting upstairs. We don’t have time for internal squabbling, do we?”

Stepping forward as if to wedge herself between the two glaring men, Rem glared at both in turn. At her stern gaze, Wilhelm bowed his head, and the giant figure—the old giant calling himself Old Man Rom—also cleared his throat and showed a willingness to follow Rem.

While grateful for Rem’s judgment in mediating, Otto couldn’t help but feel a certain sense of understanding toward the bitter exchange he just witnessed.

――Otto was also a citizen of this Dragonfriend Kingdom of Lugunica.

He knew the fact that ‘Sword Demon’ Wilhelm van Astrea was a hero of the ‘Demi-Human War,’ and that Barga Cromwell was one of the commanders of the Demi-Human Alliance during that civil war.

He had never imagined that Barga Cromwell was still alive.

Of course, Old Man Rom himself denied any connection to Barga, and would likely never admit it.

In any case――

“Allow me to call you Rom-san… We are grateful that you dispatched Wilhelm-san as reinforcements. Without that, we would have been annihilated by now.”

“I wouldn’t call that an exaggeration. If you’d been captured by the castle in your current state—being neither a royal selection candidate nor a knight—they could easily erase you and cover it up however they like.”

“Easily erase, that’s…”

“We must assume the worst possibility. Disliking it and escaping into optimism doesn’t mean the opponent has any reason to go easy on us. …Especially now that Miklotov is dead.”

Rem was left speechless by Old Man Rom’s words, which treated the situation gravely, but Otto agreed.

Always assume the worst possibilities. In the end, that’s what leads to finding a path to survival in a desperate situation. Even he himself thought it was pessimistic, but still.

“Hey, Wilhelm-san, ye saved my ass back there.”

At that, Garfiel, sitting near the wall, raised a hand lightly to Wilhelm. At the call, Wilhelm turned, “Garfiel-dono,” and said,

“I apologize that my skill was insufficient in that situation. Unless I took you by surprise, willing to cut you down as well, I could not land a blow on Reinhard.”

“I braced myself for that and took it, so no worries. The wound from that is already almost closed up. …The one from the ‘Sword Saint’s’ hand chop, though, is still nowhere near healed.”

“――――”

“More’n that, what were ye doin’, Wilhelm-san? I heard our boss and the Duchess over there were escapin’ together…”

“Indeed. Allow me to explain what happened on my side.”

With that, Wilhelm solemnly began to recount what had happened to him, and to his lord Crusch, up to this point.

“After Subaru-dono and Emilia-sama visited the mansion and departed, Crusch-sama, having seen them off, secluded herself in her room. Neither I nor any of the household could approach, and she hardly took any meals.”

“That… must have been worrying.”

“Indeed. Everyone understood that this could not continue. So, I sought the assistance of the former duke, Meckart Karsten-sama, Crusch-sama’s father, and was away from the mansion preparing for that. However, during that absence――”

“――Crusch-sama left the mansion alone and headed for the estate of Miklotov McMahon-dono.”

“Precisely. By the time it reached my ears, it was already too late.”

With an expression of undisguised regret, Wilhelm lamented his own inadequacy.

However, if Crusch had deliberately timed her departure for when Wilhelm was absent, it would have only been a matter of sooner or later, and there was no reason for him to be blamed.

That said, given the outcome was this situation, the ‘Sword Demon’s’ self-reproach was understandable.

“Naturally, I could not imagine Crusch-sama resorting to such a reckless act. I immediately went to the Royal Castle and appealed to an old acquaintance, Bordeaux Zellgef-dono. However, not only was I refused an ear, but I ended up being pursued by soldiers on my way back. At that point――”

“――I called out to him. Frankly, it was an agonizing choice for me.”

“……It was also not my intention to cut down Royal Kingdom soldiers and force my way through. I could not believe my eyes when I saw this man in the light of day.”

“Both of you.”

The inextinguishable anger and fated connection inevitably mixed venom into their words.

As Rem sharply scolded the two men, Otto understood the circumstances of their reunion. He also understood the process leading up to Wilhelm’s joining them.

“In that case, what about you, Rom-san? You seem to have had things remarkably well prepared, or rather, made very quick decisions.”

“It’s only natural you’d be suspicious, but I could only move just before you all as well; it’s much the same. The reason I noticed was because my nose is sharp… I’ve had a sixth sense for approaching danger since the old days. It’d gotten rusty for a while, but the recent turmoil seems to have scraped the rust off.”

“I see, is that so. ――Understood.”

Rolling his large shoulders, Old Man Rom replied matter-of-factly. Otto decided not to pry further.

Right now, they just happened to be facing the same direction; positionally, they were from opposing camps. It was natural for him to keep his cards close to his chest, and criticizing that would be narrow-minded.

At the very least, Old Man Rom’s actions had saved Otto and the others from a crisis. For now, he should prioritize evaluating those actions over doubting their true intent.

“A scary young fellow, aren’t ya. Your eyes aren’t smiling at all.”

“My apologies. A merchant’s fundamental principle is to smile outwardly while smirking inwardly, but lately, I’ve been unable to act very merchant-like. I disgust myself. ――Although, if a good-natured merchant lets his family die, then such a person is unnecessary right now.”

“――――”

“……Apologies, I spoke out of turn.”

After shrugging and replying, Otto chastised himself for those extra words.

If it was just thinking it, fine, but speaking it aloud made it a weapon. If you suddenly draw a weapon while facing someone, you can’t complain about being stabbed repeatedly.

Indeed, more than he had thought, being outmatched in his ‘Divine Protection of Soul Language’ was lingering within him. He had told himself like a curse that entrusting his identity to his Divine Protection was dangerous, yet recently he had relied on it too much. This was the price.

“――In any case, we here share the same position. Our lords have been unjustly slandered, and the Royal Castle tolerates it… no, rather, is leading the charge. Their aim is to eliminate the royal selection candidates, destroy the very rules of the royal selection, and dominate the kingdom.”

“And for that, Emilia-san, and that person too, are being spoken ill of… The ones Wilhelm-san and Rom-san support as well, is that it?”

“Emilia-sama, Felt-sama, the Duchess… so that leaves just Anastasia-sama and the church’s new candidate, Falaire-sama, huh.”

“I wonder about that. If the ‘Sages’ Council’ and the participants of the half-round table are willing to use any means, there are plenty of ways to slander Anastasia-sama. Since Anastasia-sama is from Kararagi, perhaps they’d claim she’s arranging for the city-state to invade the kingdom… or that she conspired with Emilia-sama in the Volakian Empire to assassinate Priscilla-sama――”

“――Don’t you dare jest!”

Rem raised her voice angrily at Otto’s speculation of such a malicious plot.

Her light-blue eyes moist, breathing heavily, she clenched her fists tightly, exposing her fury at the slanderous notion of using Priscilla’s death – her demise – in such a way.

“I will absolutely not allow them to slander and exploit Priscilla-san’s death. If they seriously say something like that, I will not forgive it…! If it reaches Abel-san’s ears, it will mean war with Volakia!”

“Actually, it’s not entirely a joke. Slighting Emilia-sama, who brought back the achievement of forging a friendship treaty with the Empire, is akin to throwing mud on the face of the Empire that recognized her. A ridiculous reason for war, but history is full of such ridiculous reasons. Moreover…”

“――Even if it did come to war, Reinhard is here. Controlling the Royal Castle means being able to move the ‘Sword Saint.’ It seems the authority to issue orders to the ‘Sword Saint’ was strictly managed to prevent such things until now… but the enemy has obtained it.”

“That’s… impossible…”

While it was truly the worst possible scenario, Old Man Rom did not deny Otto’s thoughts but instead paved the nightmare by filling in the gaps.

At the sheer terror of it, Rem and Garfiel, who had just barely escaped a single exchange with Reinhard with their lives, were at a loss for words.

Only one person――

“――As I thought. The ‘Divine Protection of the Sword Saint,’ is it.”

――muttered the ‘Sword Demon’ in a voice so low that almost no one could hear it.

“……Judging by the situation, it’s clear the enemy has the will to attack the royal selection. That being the case, we must assume that Falaire-sama, who recently appeared on the stage, and the ‘Divine Dragon Church’ supporting her are on the enemy’s side. To confirm, about the princess who vanished fifteen years ago…”

“――Felt is Felt. There is no other answer.”

Disliking the stagnation the silence brought to their discussion, Otto’s attempt to organize the situation and confirm facts was cut off, hard and clear, by Old Man Rom’s words.

Perhaps thinking it was too unkind to end it with just that denial over the question, Old Man Rom added “Still” to the surrounding gazes,

“That story of the ‘Divine Dragon Church’ sheltering the lost princess sounds like a tall tale to me. Even keeping a distance from the Royal Castle, to conceal that matter for over a year since the royal selection began… that’s unthinkable in a crisis threatening the kingdom’s very existence.”

Juxtaposing a firm opinion with an uncertain attitude, Old Man Rom was clearly hiding something.

Naturally, the ‘Sword Demon’s’ gaze directed at the old giant grew sharper.

“――――”

Wilhelm, who had been the captain of the Royal Guard Knights fifteen years ago at the time, was said to have been responsible for the search for the vanished princess. This time, his desire to know the answer regarding the princess suspicion cast over Felt and Falaire was likely stronger than anyone’s.

However, the mettle of the man suspected of being one of the Three Great Chiefs of the Demi-Human Alliance was not so fragile as to crack under the obsession dwelling in that sharp gaze.

In any case――

“……I understand how bad the situation is.”

Exhaling softly, Rem straightened her back firmly, seemingly forcing a shift in her feelings. Then, she looked around at the members gathered in the room—Otto and the others—in turn,

“Frankly, I’m extremely worried about that person who isn’t here right now, but Emilia-san and Sister in the castle are in danger, aren’t they? How on earth do we get them out… no, Felt-san too. How do we get them out?”

“If Reinhard and the Knight Commander are over there, a frontal assault’s just too unreasonable, no matter what. It’d be like ‘Gaddogi Guaddzeadd’s mountain retreat.’ We need a plan, Otto-nii.”

Garfiel, heavily burdened from his fight with Reinhard, agreed with Rem’s opinion and looked to Otto with eyes expecting a strategy from here on out.

For the two of them, Emilia, confined in the castle, was of course a worry, and even more so, they had to be anxious about the safety of Ram, who had accompanied her as an attendant.

Telling them this was truly painful, but――

“――No. From now on, we will prioritize escaping from the Royal Capital. We have no leeway to extract Emilia-sama and Ram-san from the Royal Castle, nor Felt-sama.”

““Wha――!?””

Eyes wide with shock, Garfiel and Rem raised their voices simultaneously. Immediately, Garfiel stood up, using the wall for support, and barked, “Otto-nii!”

“Escape… yer sayin’ we’re not goin’ to help them… what’s that supposed to mean!”

“It means exactly what I said. At present, we lack both the means and the fighting strength to extract Emilia-sama and the others imprisoned in the castle. A half-baked plan would just be crushed by brute force, and we’d all fall into enemy hands together. We cannot fight such a losing battle.”

“A losing battle… But, Sister is there, Emilia-san is…”

“I understand. However, even if the enemy has already taken control of the Royal Castle, they cannot casually lay hands on a royal selection candidate. Even Reinhard-san, who follows their orders, couldn’t overlook such a move. Their freedom will be restricted, but as long as they are in the castle, there is a high possibility that Emilia-sama and the others will not be harmed. That is my assessment.”

“B-but, still…”

Otto, striving to remain as calm as possible, carefully kept emotion from his voice, but Garfiel and Rem, their raw emotions exposed, were deeply shaken. However, into this exchange, Old Man Rom raised a large hand and interjected, “May I?”

